---
/**
 * Terms of sale.
 *
 * Separate from /terms-of-use, which governs reading the site. This governs
 * buying something, which brings the Australian Consumer Law with it: consumer
 * guarantees that cannot be contracted out of, a single price inclusive of GST,
 * and an accurate account of delivery and returns.
 *
 * Drafted, not approved. It carries the draft notice and sits on the register
 * as awaiting-legal alongside the privacy policy and the terms of use. The shop
 * should not open to the public until a lawyer has read this page.
 *
 * Two things on it need a person rather than a developer: the returns window,
 * which is a decision and not a law, and the tax invoice wording, which the
 * accountant should confirm against what Stripe actually sends.
 */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import DraftNotice from '../../components/DraftNotice.astro';
import { CHURCH } from '../../data/church.mjs';
import { SHIPPING, postingAvailable } from '../../lib/shop.mjs';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Shop terms"
  description="Terms of sale for merchandise from The Transformation Edge: prices, GST, delivery, exchanges and refunds."
  route="shop/terms"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Shop', href: '/shop' }]}
  standfirst="What you are agreeing to when you buy something here."
  noindex
>
  <DraftNotice what="These sale terms need a legal review before the shop opens, plus two decisions: how long the change-of-mind window runs, and the exact tax invoice wording the accountant wants Stripe to send." />

  <div class="terms prose">
    <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
    <p>
      {CHURCH.legalName}, ABN <span class="ltr-embed">{CHURCH.abn}</span>, of{' '}
      {CHURCH.address.unit}, {CHURCH.address.street}, {CHURCH.address.suburb}{' '}
      {CHURCH.address.state} <span class="ltr-embed">{CHURCH.address.postcode}</span>.
    </p>

    <h2>Prices and GST</h2>
    <p>
      Every price shown includes GST. The figure on the product page is the figure you pay for
      that item, and delivery, where it applies, is shown separately before you pay.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are registered for GST, so your receipt from Stripe shows the GST component and carries
      our ABN. Keep it: that is your tax invoice.
    </p>

    <h2>Paying</h2>
    <p>
      Payment is handled by Stripe on Stripe's own pages. No payment details are entered on this
      site and we never see or hold them. Your order is placed when Stripe confirms the payment,
      not when you add something to a basket.
    </p>
    <p>
      If an item is listed at an obviously wrong price, we will contact you and either refund you
      in full or ask whether you want it at the right price. We will not simply charge you more.
    </p>

    <h2>Getting your order</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>{SHIPPING.collect.label}.</strong> Free. {SHIPPING.collect.note} Ask at the welcome
      desk. We do not need a postal address for a collection, so we do not ask for one.
    </p>
    {
      postingAvailable() ? (
        <p>
          <strong>{SHIPPING.post.label}.</strong> {SHIPPING.post.note} {SHIPPING.post.estimate}{' '}
          Postage is charged at a flat rate shown before you pay. We post within Australia only.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          <strong>Posting.</strong> Not available yet. Orders are collected at our Sunday
          gathering for now.
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p>
      Delivery estimates are estimates. Once an order is with the carrier, its timing is not
      something we control, though we will chase anything that goes astray.
    </p>

    <h2>Sizes, exchanges and changing your mind</h2>
    <p>
      Apparel can be exchanged for a different size where we have it, unworn and unwashed, with
      the receipt. Get in touch first so we can put the size aside rather than you making a trip
      for nothing.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not required to refund a change of mind, and for a small range like this one we
      generally offer an exchange rather than a refund. That does not affect anything in the next
      section.
    </p>

    <h2>If something is faulty, damaged or wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Tell us and we will put it right. Depending on how serious the problem is, that means a
      repair, a replacement or a refund, and we pay the cost of returning it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our goods come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law.
      You are entitled to a replacement or a refund for a major failure and to compensation for
      any other reasonably foreseeable loss or damage. You are also entitled to have the goods
      repaired or replaced if they fail to be of acceptable quality and the failure does not
      amount to a major failure. Nothing on this page limits those rights.
    </p>
    <p>Refunds go back to the card or account used to pay, through Stripe.</p>

    <h2>What we hold about an order</h2>
    <p>
      For a collection we hold your name and your email address. For a posted order we also hold
      the delivery address and a phone number for the carrier. Stripe holds the payment record.
      Our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> says how long we keep things and who to
      ask about them.
    </p>

    <h2>This is a purchase, not a gift</h2>
    <p>
      Buying merchandise supports our church, but it is a purchase. It is not a deductible gift
      and no gift receipt is issued for it. If you meant to give, the{' '}
      <a href="/give">giving page</a> is the place, and it explains how receipting works there.
    </p>

    <h2>Getting hold of us</h2>
    <p>
      Call <a href={`tel:${CHURCH.phoneE164}`} class="ltr-embed">{CHURCH.phone}</a>, email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CHURCH.email}`}>{CHURCH.email}</a>, or use the{' '}
      <a href="/get-in-touch">contact page</a>. Somebody reads everything that comes in and
      replies within two working days.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .terms {
    max-inline-size: var(--measure);
  }

  .terms h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .terms h2:first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }
</style>
